CAPS9 = {
"97_tab_morning": ("B2C","Ten minutes before anything else.\n\nWeigh-in, hip flow, thoracic opener, a walk outside. Not a second app, not a separate document: a tab in the same plan.\n\nAnd if you didn't ask for a morning routine, the tab simply isn't there. You only get what applies to you.","general"),
"98_tab_fuel": ("B2C","Nutrition, sat next to the training it's fuelling.\n\nMeals, timings and macros for the day, a shape to eat around, not something to follow to the gram.\n\nNot interested? Say so and the tab never appears. We're not going to make you look at it 🍳","general"),
"99_tab_recover": ("B2C","Recovery is programmed, not left to good intentions.\n\nSleep target, what to do after a session, which days are genuinely rest days, and week four dropping volume so the fitness you built can actually show up.\n\nTraining is the stimulus. This is where the adaptation happens 😴","general"),
"100_app_timer_running": ("B2C","Stop timing your rest on a phone stopwatch.\n\nThree minutes on the squat. Sixty seconds on calves. The timer's already set to what that exercise needs, so you don't have to remember which is which.\n\nTap the set and it counts you down ⏱️","general"),
"101_week_one_vs_three": ("B2C","Week one and week three, same session, side by side.\n\nSame movements. Same order. Ten kilos on the squat.\n\nThat's what progressive overload actually looks like written down, not a new programme every fortnight. Familiarity is the feature 📈","strength"),
"102_deload_week": ("B2C","What a deload actually looks like.\n\nThree sets at roughly 80% of week three. Enough to keep the pattern and the habit, little enough that accumulated fatigue clears.\n\nNot a week off. Not the same week lighter for no reason. Then you test, and the next block starts from a real number.","strength"),
"103_upper_vs_lower": ("B2C","What an upper day and a lower day should actually contain.\n\nA heavy compound, then support work for whatever it didn't cover. That's the whole logic.\n\nPulling goes first on upper days, because almost everyone already has more pressing volume than pulling, and whatever you do first gets your best effort.","strength"),
"104_phases_view": ("B2B","Physios, structure by phase, not by weekday.\n\nPhase 1 tolerance, Phase 2 capacity, Phase 3 load, Phase 4 consolidate. Your patient moves on when they're ready, not when the calendar says so.\n\nA calendar doesn't know whether they're ready. You do.\n\nYou build it, you approve it. Clinical judgement stays entirely with you. DM me for a look 👋","physios"),
"105_part_done": ("B2C","Halfway through and it knows exactly where you are.\n\nPut your phone down between sets, pick it up, carry on. Nothing to re-find, nothing to scroll back through.\n\nBuilt to be used in a gym, not read at a desk.","product"),
"106_coach_client_view": ("B2B","Coaches, this is what your client opens on Monday morning.\n\nYour programme, your notes attached to the exercises they matter for. The single-leg work is before the calf raise on purpose, and the note says why.\n\nYour coaching, in a format they'll actually open on the gym floor.\n\nDM me for a look, five minutes, no pitch.","coaches"),
"107_hotel_fuel": ("B2C","Eating well away from home, without pretending you've got a kitchen.\n\nHotel buffet. Whatever's near. A protein source and something green. That's the whole rule.\n\nTwo weeks of imperfect eating changes nothing. Two weeks of stressing about it ruins the trip ✈️","general"),
"108_whole_block": ("B2C","You can see the whole block from day one.\n\nEvery week is there the moment you buy it. Look ahead if you want to. Screenshot it, print it, keep it.\n\nNo drip feed, nothing expiring, nothing renewing. You paid once. It's yours.","product"),
}
